MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Fall of Ideals feels like a natural next choice because melodic guitar lines paired with harsh vocals connect closely to my listening to In Flames and Soilwork.",
    "Vol. 3, City of Evil, and The Crusade fit my interest in music that combines aggression with memorable melodies or intricate riffs, connecting my heavier listening with my interest in accessible hard rock."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Testify feels less relevant because its rap-rock direction does not give me the melodic metal sound I want right now, even though it shares the intensity of other albums here.",
    "Stone Sour, Lost and Found, and Faceless fit parts of my taste, but heaviness and strong grooves alone are not enough to make them my first choices today."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat heavy riffs and aggression as stronger signs of what I want than they are on their own.",
    "My interest in accessible hard rock seems to have been carried too broadly into nearby styles, especially rap-rock."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated listening to In Flames and Soilwork points to a particular combination of melodic guitar work and harsh vocals that matters more to me than heaviness alone.",
    "Advance And Vanquish and my recent Tool listening make intricate, engaging instrumental work especially appealing; that helps explain why City of Evil and The Crusade stand out over other plausible matches."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in heavy music, but only some captured the melody, vocal contrast, and intricate riffs that make me choose an album right now."
}
